 ### Generator Architecture
 *   **Definition:** A generator network $G(r, z)$ that maps a sinogram $r$ and a latent vector $z$ to a reconstructed image, used for optimization in the inverse problem [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Layout:** The input sinogram $r$ passes through an Embedding Conv 2D layer and U-Net Blocks. The latent vector $z$ is processed by a 'Modified Block' and integrated into the network. The architecture is analogous to the end-to-end reconstruction model but includes this latent injection mechanism [S1, unofficial].
